11	/**
12	 * Tripwires for the 2026-07-27 HTTP API surface audit.
13	 *
14	 * Two defect classes, both confirmed against the running production server
15	 * before they were fixed:
16	 *
17	 *   1. Every per-IP rate limit keyed on the FIRST hop of `X-Forwarded-For`.
18	 *      nginx is configured with `$proxy_add_x_forwarded_for`, which APPENDS the
19	 *      real peer, so the first hop is whatever the caller typed. Proven live:
20	 *        curl -H 'X-Forwarded-For: 203.0.113.77' https://nxeon.cloud/api/tools/my-ip
21	 *        → {"ip":"203.0.113.77","forwardedFor":"203.0.113.77, 127.0.0.1"}
22	 *      One header per request bought an unlimited budget on every throttled
23	 *      endpoint, including the ones that spend money (Claude, the registrar).
24	 *
25	 *   2. Per-customer and credential-bearing JSON went out with NO `Cache-Control`
26	 *      at all, which lets a shared cache assign heuristic freshness (RFC 9111
27	 *      §4.2.2) and replay one caller's body to the next.
28	 *
29	 * Deterministic: no network, no DB, no clock. Nothing here imports a route
30	 * module — that would pull in Prisma and open a connection to the production
31	 * database — so the cache-header checks assert against route SOURCE instead.
32	 */
33	
34	const HERE = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));
35	const API_DIR = path.join(HERE, "..", "app", "api");
