14	/**
15	 * The four authentication defects from the 2026-07-26 customer-journey
16	 * rehearsal (docs/QA-JOURNEY.md B4, H6, H7, M3).
17	 *
18	 * They share one shape, and it is not the shape of a typo: each one is a door
19	 * that reports itself open and is not. Correct credentials that never sign you
20	 * in. A reset link that is promised and never sent. A password that satisfies
21	 * the rule it is rejected for. An account that can spend money at an address
22	 * nobody has ever proved they can read. None of them throws, none of them logs,
23	 * and none of them is visible to the person they trap.
24	 *
25	 * Two of the four live in React rendering and one lives in a live Postgres
26	 * unique index, so neither can be exercised from a unit test. The policy that
27	 * decides them, though, is pure — and that half is tested for real below. The
28	 * source tripwires cover the rest: weaker than a browser, immeasurably stronger
29	 * than nothing, and they fail the moment the shape that caused the incident
30	 * reappears.
