/**
 * Bearer-token authentication for the public REST API (`/api/v1/*`).
 *
 * TWO customer-facing credential models exist and BOTH are accepted here —
 * this is not indecision, it's a migration in progress:
 *
 *   - `ApiToken` (`nxe_<prefix>_<random>`): the richer model — array `scopes`
 *     with wildcard support (`*`, `resource:*`, generic `read`), `expiresAt`,
 *     and it's what the admin user-detail page already displays
 *     (`app/admin/users/[id]/page.tsx`). `lib/actions-tokens.ts` can create and
 *     revoke these end-to-end, but as of 2026-09-24 nothing reachable in the
 *     live customer UI calls it — its one intended entry point,
 *     `components/customer/SecuritySettings.tsx`, is orphaned (no page
 *     imports it, a leftover from before the Nexion redesign).
 *
 *   - `ApiKey` (`nxk_live_<random>`): what Settings (`app/dashboard/settings`)
 *     ACTUALLY creates today, via `createApiKey` in lib/nx/account.ts — the
 *     only customer-reachable path to a working key. Its `scope` is a single
 *     string (`"full" | "servers:read" | "metrics:read"`, coarser than
 *     ApiToken's array), and it has no `expiresAt` column.
 *
 * Before this fix, this function only ever recognised `nxe_` — so every key a
 * customer generated from Settings (`nxk_live_…`) authenticated as "Invalid
 * token format" against every route, permanently, with no error anywhere
